//Concurrency import redesign: `import thread;` makes the package's
//Thread declaration visible in this TU, and a same-name user class now
//collides with it (the duplicate-field check) instead of silently
//shadowing as it did when Thread was prelude-owned — implicit prelude
//names yield to user declarations, explicitly imported ones do not
//(the Java single-type-import rule). compile_error pins the collision.
import thread;

class Thread {
}

int main() {
    return 0;
}
